<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1979</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Revolutionary Guards, IRGC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps is a branch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>'s armed forces founded in 1979 to protect the Islamic Republic and its revolution. Separate from the regular army, it grew powerful during the Iran-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> War and controls the Basij militia, ballistic missiles and the Quds Force, which supports allied armed groups abroad. It also has extensive business interests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/islamic-revolutionary-guard-corps.jpg" alt="Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps" width="320" height="341" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MrInfo2012 This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_Army_of_the_Guardians_of_the_Islamic_Revolution.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
